<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Outcome-record derivation (#1288, under #1272). Once a day it derives one
  append-only outcome record for every closed ticket in every member
  repository and appends the new ones to outcomes.jsonl on the heartbeat
  branch.

  Why this exists: outcomes.py derive had no scheduler at all between
  2026-09-13 and this job. Every signal drawn from outcomes.jsonl — the
  rework rate, first-pass approval, cost per merged PR — was therefore as
  stale as whenever somebody last ran the command by hand, while reading as
  current. An unscheduled derivation is worse than an absent one, because the
  numbers still render.

  It passes no repository list; the all-members flag asks GitHub which repositories
  carry the funnel topic, so a repository that opts in is scanned without
  anyone remembering to edit this file; see AGENTS.md, "GitHub is the state".
  The flag fails closed when that answer is empty rather than deriving
  nothing and exiting 0.

  A Python script on a timer, not a headless prompt: AGENTS.md's
  in-app-scheduling rule covers Claude Code and Codex prompt execution and
  does not reach this, which is the same reading the publisher (#652) and the
  dashboard deploy (#653) already run under.

  StartCalendarInterval at 03:20, not StartInterval: daily is a calendar
  notion, and 03:20 is off the Muse lanes' :00/:05/:15 slots, off the 07:00
  member-repo dailies, and inside the window when nothing else contends for
  the GraphQL budget this job spends.

  The canonical copy lives here in the repo. launchd refuses a symlinked
  plist (`Bootstrap failed: 5: Input/output error`, measured 2026-09-07), so
  the installed file is a copy and tests/test_launchd_drift.py compares them.

  Note for editors: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment. Use an em
  dash or a semicolon; plutil accepts the double hyphen and plistlib rejects
  it, so a file can lint clean and still be unparseable.

  After editing, re-install from a Terminal in the logged-in console session:
    cp launchd/com.nateprich.command-center-outcomes-derive.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.nateprich.command-center-outcomes-derive
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nateprich.command-center-outcomes-derive.plist
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.nateprich.command-center-outcomes-derive</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
        <string>/Users/nateprich/.claude/command-center-run/outcomes.py</string>
        <string>derive</string>
        <string>--all-members</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>3</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>20</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nateprich/Library/Logs/command-center-outcomes-derive.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nateprich/Library/Logs/command-center-outcomes-derive.err.log</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/nateprich/.local/bin</string>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/nateprich</string>
    </dict>

    <key>ProcessType</key>
    <string>Background</string>
</dict>
</plist>
